# THE CLAIMS THAT SPAN A WIDTH, WHEREVER IN A DOCUMENT THEY SIT. One row per claim whose low
# and high differ, so there is something a narrowing statement could actually reduce.
#
# ⭐⭐ THIS IS THE DENOMINATOR FOR EVERY QUESTION ABOUT UNCERTAINTY IN A FILING. Judging
#    whether a narrowing sentence WOULD narrow the range is prose and belongs to a person.
#    Counting how many ranges decline to say anything at all is arithmetic, and it turns
#    "a claim without one is weaker" from an opinion into a figure.
#
# ⛔ AND THE MIRROR OF THE POINT RULE LIVES HERE: a range filing `narrowsWhen` as
#   `notApplicable` is claiming it has no range, in a row that demonstrably has one.
-- pm:Claim where low <> high, at every element that carries one.
SELECT c.*
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/claims.sqlc)
) c
WHERE NOT c.is_a_point
